Description

We are seeking an experienced Project Manager to support a major provincial healthcare transformation initiative in New Brunswick, focused on implementing a unified Clinical Information Solution (CIS).

Key Responsibilities

Develop and maintain integrated project schedules and delivery forecasts;
Coordinate activities, milestones, dependencies, and resources across multiple workstreams;
Organize project meetings, prepare agendas, document decisions, and track action items;
Maintain project documentation, risk logs, and status reports;
Monitor schedule progress, identify risks and variances, and escalate issues;
Support project governance, stakeholder coordination, and knowledge transfer, etc;

Required Qualifications

Post-secondary education in a health-related field or equivalent relevant experience;
2+ years of project scheduling and coordination experience within a CIS, healthcare, or digital health environment;
Experience managing multiple stakeholders, workstreams, and governance activities;
Strong knowledge of Microsoft Office 365 and JIRA;

Assets

Experience with clinical information systems and large-scale healthcare transformation projects;
Bilingual English/French (written and verbal);
Formal project management or process improvement training (Prosci, APMP, Lean Six Sigma, or equivalent).

Engagement Details

2-year independent consulting engagement (not a salaried position);
Primarily remote, ability to travel to New Brunswick at least once per month is required.

Reference: RQ00403 Project Coordinator – Scheduler

